          "title": "DASH DIET AND ITS ROLE IN THE PREVENTION OF HYPERTENSION AND METABOLIC SYNDROME",
          "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20513332",
          "publication_date": "2026-06-02",
          "description": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;Hypertension and metabolic syndrome are among the leading non-communicable diseases worldwide and represent major public health challenges. Dietary interventions play a crucial role in reducing cardiovascular risk factors and improving overall health outcomes. The Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension (DASH) diet has been widely recognized as an effective nutritional strategy for lowering blood pressure and improving metabolic health. This article reviews the principles of the DASH diet and summarizes its effects on hypertension and metabolic syndrome based on current scientific evidence.</p>",
